From fd059cc61742a8d83b033c8c1113f9383fb45e25 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nuubOS <nuubos@localhost>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 21:05:23 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 08/11] ARM64 dynarec: wait loops, direct memory access
 (nuubOS)

Wait loops: when a short backward conditional branch that writes no
memory is taken and the SH4 registers (r0-r15, pr, T, gbr, mac, fpul) are
the same as the time before, the loop only waits for memory something
else changes (an interrupt handler, DMA, the AICA), so the rest of the
time slice is spent at once. Shenmue II spent 27 % of its emulation
thread in one that the single-block idle detector misses (a counter
compared with a target around an empty callback). Loops whose state
seldom repeats (fewer than 1 in 16 of 4096 checks) stop being checked;
a wrong guess only costs emulated time, events still come in order.

Direct memory access: without the MMU and with the 4 GB mapping, reads
and writes go straight from the address register to the destination (or
from the source) register, 3 instructions instead of 5 (no copies
through w0/w1); ngen_Rewrite reads the registers back from the add and
the load/store it replaces (the plain accesses are rn 0, rt 0 or 1). The
SH4 thread is bound by the Cortex-A53's instruction cache.

Conditional block ends compare w29 (jcond/jdyn leave the condition
there) instead of reloading jdyn from the context.

Upstream: not submitted (nuubOS H700 tuning).
---
 core/hw/sh4/dyna/blockmanager.h |   4 +
 core/hw/sh4/dyna/decoder.cpp    |  11 ++
 core/rec-ARM64/rec_arm64.cpp    | 207 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 3 files changed, 218 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/core/hw/sh4/dyna/blockmanager.h b/core/hw/sh4/dyna/blockmanager.h
